Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 16:45:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fix(read): range R2 objects and drop OPFS plaintext

Context:
Source PR #111 Greptile on 7f8d93f4 found three in-scope issues:
R2 Range responses buffered the full object; OPFS staging left
decrypted plaintext and unrevoked object URLs; 416 omitted CORS
exposure of Content-Range.

Expected behavior:
Unencrypted R2 GET with a simple byte Range uses R2 ranged get and
returns 206 without buffering the whole object. OPFS staging removes
the temporary file after creating the object URL, and the Display
download revokes that URL. Unsatisfiable ranges expose Content-Range.

Acceptance criteria:
- R2 Range 206 returns only the requested bytes.
- OPFS removeEntry is called after staging.
- 416 includes Access-Control-Expose-Headers: Content-Range.

Constraints:
- Encrypted pastes still ignore Range.
- No P2P, ZIP, or max-read consume.

Validation:
- TDD: RED missing R2 Range / OPFS removeEntry / 416 CORS expose;
  GREEN after ranged R2 get, OPFS cleanup, and 416 headers.
- vitest run: 23 files / 164 tests PASS
- lint / typecheck / Prettier PASS

Docs:
- worker/test/range.spec.ts
- frontend/test/opfs.spec.ts

Refs:
- Issue #82
- Source PR #111
- Greptile P1/P2 on 7f8d93f4bc8d6fe320bb0c23a801451244922fe3

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
